     {
       "id": "stas_soiltype02",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 real-data run over the Colorado Rockies (8.1 km, 18 h, data/eqwefic/gwdo_real, dumped by ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-gwdo), at a column whose soil category is 2 (loamy sand). smcmax, smcref, smcwlt and smcdry are REDPRM's own outputs for that column, dumped by WRF, so this is an INDEPENDENT end-to-end check of the SOILPARM lookup -- a different run, a different executable and a different land-use table from the one the component's table was taken from. Only soil quantities are asserted: that run uses the 20-category MODIS vegetation table (isurban = 13), not the USGS table this component carries, so its vegtyp indexes a different table and its vegetation parameters are deliberately NOT compared. Values are real32 from a single-precision WRF build, hence rel 1e-7 rather than the 1e-12 used against the kernel replay.",
       "parameter_overrides": {
         "soiltyp": 2.0,
         "vegtyp": 2.0,
         "slopetyp": 1.0,
         "shdfac": 0.3568728566169739,
